Hoffman was a high ranking official and loyal follower of [[the Professor]]. After the Professor's defeat, he became a joined the team of [[Mr. Wilder|Mr. Mr. Wilder]] and supported him in his campaign to become the new leader of the Organization. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Hoffman was with [[Mr. Wilder]] and [[Stack]] at the South American Forest in Peru. He fought [[Dante Vale]] outside the waterfall cave that hid the [[Nexus]] but retreated with Mr. Wilder
when [[Myrmidon]] was defeated. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

At [[Tower of Nostradamus]], Hoffman defeated the three Huntik operatives stationed there, first [[Billie]]  and [[Peter]], and right after that [[Annette]] while she was dialing for help. When Dante's team arrived, Hoffman fought against [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]]  but was thrown out of the tower by the enchanted [[Sentry Triclops]] Titans. {{Source|The Tower of Nostradamus}}

Hoffman then was sent to the Chu Goku Mount, Japan, with [[Eathon the dog]] to find the [[Amulet]] of [[Divine Mirror Kagami]]. He took the Amulet to [[Avalon]] and fought against Dante, who was turned to stone when Kagami's ability reflected the Stonegaze ability of [[King Basilisk]]. When [[Zhalia Moon]] reversed the ability and returned Dante to normal, Hoffman retreated with [[Stack]]. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}

Hoffman was with Mr. Wilder's team when Lok, Sophie and [[Cherit]] were captured. He left with Mr. Wilder, leaving Stack and the remaining team with the mission of escorting Lok, Sophie and Cherit to Organization HQ. {{source|Chasing Void}}

Hoffman, alongside Mr. Wilder and Stack, ambushed the Huntik team in [[Klaus' laboratory]]. He fought against Lok and Sophie, but was defeated through the aid of Cherit before the Organization was ambushed by the [[Blood Spiral]]. {{source|The Blood Spiral}}

He and Mr. Wilder observed Stack attempting to infiltrate the Blood Spiral on Medusa Island. When Dante's team arrived, Hoffman summoned [[Myrmidon]] to fight alongside a Suit's [[Venomaster]] against Dante's [[Caliban]]. Meanwhile, Hoffman fought against Sophie and [[Sabriel]] but, upon defeat, retreated with Mr. Wilder, leaving Stack behind. {{source|Zhalia's Mission}}

At the vault of [[Hernán Cortés]], Hoffman and Mr. Wilder set few new traps for Dante and his team, capturing [[Den Fears]] in a [[Trapcage]] spell. Hoffman fought Den, Lok, and Sophie, but retreated when Dante obtained the Ring of [[Umbra]] the Shadow Jaguar, trapping the Huntik Foundation in the cave with [[Conquistador]]. {{source|The Power of Umbra}}

When the Huntik team went looking for [[Rassimov]]'s secret files in [[the Professor's castle]], Hoffman and Mr. Wilder were at that base. Hoffman and [[Eathon the dog]] fought against Dante and [[Grier]], but he was eventually subdued and defeated. Afterwards, Hoffman was left to guard the castle when Grier took Mr. Wilder hostage and took control of the Organization. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}

[[File:S2E35_Hoffman.png|thumb|200px]]
As a loyal member of the Organization, Hoffman took orders from his superiors without hesitation. Due to this loyalty, he was well-liked by the Professor and thoroughly despised traitors. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}} Shunning cowardice, he values resolution and determination. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}} Due to his strong resolve, Hoffman can be stubborn when it comes to him making up his mind. {{Source|An Ally from the Organization}} However, unlike the lower [[Suits]], Hoffman can weigh the odds of a confrontation and knows when it is more rational to avoid the direct approach. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}  He also is not a believer in superstition. {{source|The Tower of Nostradamus}} Hoffman possesses knowledge of history. {{source|The Power of Umbra}}  

Hoffman has an extreme loyalty and respect for [[the Professor]] as shown when he took custody of [[Eathon the dog]] and when he tried to stop the Huntik Foundation from entering [[the Professor's castle]]. {{Source|Knight of the Willblade}} {{source|An Ally from the Organization}} He would not take any disresepct that the Professor needed lies to control anyone, defending him stating that the man had absolute power. {{source|Chasing Void}}

